":16,"h":32,"s":20,"a":85,"sd":null},{"k":"20:86","t":"So Moses returned to his people, angry and grieved. He said, \"O my people, did your Lord not make you a good promise? Then, was the time [of its fulfillment] too long for you, or did you wish that wrath from your Lord descend upon you, so you broke your promise [of obedience] to me?\"","j":16,"h":32,"s":20,"a":86,"sd":null},{"k":"20:87","t":"They said, \"We did not break our promise to you by our will, but we were made to carry burdens from the ornaments of the people [of Pharaoh], so we threw them [into the fire], and thus did the Sāmirī throw.\"","j":16,"h":32,"s":20,"a":87,"sd":null}],"juz":16,"hizb":32,"surahs":[20],"sajdah":false}